{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "central_D_lon_zero_grad_bc",
    "description": "Centered first derivative along longitude with zero-gradient boundary conditions on the latlon grid — the esm-spec 9.6.8 worked example, generalized over NLON/NLAT metaparameters and the consumer-supplied spacing free name. Matches D(f, wrt: lon), a PER-DEGREE derivative (see grids/latlon/grid.esm for the physical-units metric recipe). Interior columns [2, NLON-1]: the imported centered-difference stencil. Face columns i=1 and i=NLON: one-sided differences (f[2,j]-f[1,j])/dlon_deg and (f[NLON,j]-f[NLON-1,j])/dlon_deg encoding the zero-gradient condition. The three regions tile the axes, so the discretized derivative is fully defined with its BC (there is nowhere else a boundary condition could live). This is the REGIONAL boundary choice — a zero-gradient frame for a limited-area lon extent; on the global recipe the zonal circle closes and central_D_lon_periodic is the physical rule (a zero gradient on a closed circle is an artificial seam). `dlon_deg` is a free name resolving to the consuming model's zonal spacing variable (consumer-supplied geometry contract) — the zero-gradient faces themselves are spacing-scale-invariant, so the rule serves any extent unchanged. The face values keep the rank-reduced aggregate form of the spec's worked example (output over the lat axis only, filling the (1 x NLAT) leading-axis face regions); the lat-axis rules use full-rank faces instead because rank-reduced values only fill leading-axis faces portably across bindings. Match scoping: the pattern is `wrt: lon` plus the constraint `where: {f: {shape: [lon, lat]}}` (esm-spec 9.6.1), so it fires only on the longitudinal derivative of a bare field declared over this grid's lon x lat index sets — not on any unrelated D(., wrt: lon) reusing the axis name, and, under import-edge renaming (esm-spec 9.7.7), the wrt literal and the where shape follow the renamed axis together, so two latlon instances coexist scoped to their own meshes. The constraint requires a bare shaped variable; a consumer differentiating a compound inline expression must bind it to a declared lon x lat observed first.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["esd:rule", "family:finite_difference", "grid:latlon", "op:D", "axes:lon,lat", "order:2", "stencil_width:3", "bc:zero_gradient", "spec:9.6.8"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.12 (one-sided boundary treatment)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    { "ref": "../stencils/central_D_lon_interior.esm" }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "central_D_lon_zero_grad_bc": {
      "params": ["f"],
      "match": { "op": "D", "args": ["f"], "wrt": "lon" },
      "where": { "f": { "shape": ["lon", "lat"] } },
      "body": {
        "op": "makearray",
        "args": [],
        "regions": [
          [[2, { "op": "-", "args": ["NLON", 1] }], [1, "NLAT"]],
          [[1, 1], [1, "NLAT"]],
          [["NLON", "NLON"], [1, "NLAT"]]
        ],
        "values": [
          {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "central_D_lon_interior",
            "bindings": { "f": "f" }
          },
          {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": ["j"],
            "args": ["f"],
            "ranges": { "j": { "from": "lat" } },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["f", 2, "j"] },
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["f", 1, "j"] }
                  ]
                },
                "dlon_deg"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": ["j"],
            "args": ["f"],
            "ranges": { "j": { "from": "lat" } },
            "expr": {
              "op": "/",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "-",
                  "args": [
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["f", "NLON", "j"] },
                    { "op": "index", "args": ["f", { "op": "-", "args": ["NLON", 1] }, "j"] }
                  ]
                },
                "dlon_deg"
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
